WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.062
- What are good and effective
ways to collect information

00:00:03.062 --> 00:00:04.470
on a company?

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:06.750
So from my time working as a consultant

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:09.110
and later as a project lead at McKinsey,

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:12.870
I want to share my insights,
my tips and tricks on exactly

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:14.860
this topic of company research,

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.640
which I hope will be helpful
for many of you as well.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.710
These techniques will prove very helpful

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:22.470
if you're currently
preparing for job interviews,

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:24.870
or maybe you already
signed a labor contract

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.440
and are preparing for
the first days, weeks,

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.320
or months at your new employer.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.533
This info will also be
relevant if you're a consultant

00:00:31.533 --> 00:00:34.180
who wants to prepare for a new project,

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.770
for new client and
wants to get up to speed

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.700
with this new company in a faster way.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.980
So welcome to another coffee break here

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:43.910
on my channel Firm Learning,
my name is Heinrich

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:47.010
and on my channel I want to
help you to become successful

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:49.510
in the first years of your career.

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:51.750
So with no further ado, let's get into it.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:54.380
And today I want to
share with you four tips,

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:57.050
what you can do to do
some company research.

00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:59.260
And all these tips have
in common that first

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:00.690
you can do them from home.

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:04.090
Second you don't need any
access to any databases.

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:06.367
So it's pretty much for free.

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:08.980
And third it's very easy and
straight forward to do that.

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:11.630
So also no significant
time investment required.

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:13.940
And stick until the end
because especially the last two

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.190
I think are quite juicy and important.

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:17.510
So make sure you're not missing them.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:20.630
And the first step is to
read the news on the company

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:22.830
and while this might
seem a little bit obvious

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:25.350
you would be surprised
how many people I talk to,

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:28.960
also I work with were not
even aware about the last news

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:31.007
publications about a client for instance,

00:01:31.007 --> 00:01:33.380
that we just started working for.

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:35.370
And now to go a bit beyond the obvious,

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:39.270
let me share two specific
tools that you can use to

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:41.943
really simplify and
facilitate this news research.

00:01:41.943 --> 00:01:45.020
The first tool is the
Google News platform.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:47.450
So this is a search machine from Google

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:50.150
specifically dedicated to news.

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:52.600
So if you're typing in
the name of your company,

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:54.690
here you will likely
find much better results

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:57.740
regarding the news than if you
just type in the company name

00:01:57.740 --> 00:01:59.820
in the overall Google search bar,

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:01.990
because here are all search
articles that you get

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:03.460
are news articles indeed.

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:05.010
The second is Google alerts,

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:07.320
and this is pretty cool
because here can define

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:10.527
a search term and whenever
there's a new search result

00:02:10.527 --> 00:02:14.220
on Google popping up for the
term, you would get an alert.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.480
For instance an email
that Google sends you

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.607
with the overview of all the
new articles that came out.

00:02:18.607 --> 00:02:21.530
And here you can also tailor
this to decide whether you

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:23.070
want to have this really live whenever

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:24.390
something new comes in,

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:26.600
or whether you want to have
a collection of results

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:28.360
once a day or once per week.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:30.920
Depending on how common
your search term is

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:33.080
you might want to go for
the one or the other.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:35.210
But this is really something
I would recommend you to do

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:37.030
also for your current employer,

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:39.490
or maybe also your current client project

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:40.323
that you are doing.

00:02:40.323 --> 00:02:42.880
Make sure that you have
a Google alert activated,

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:45.530
and this can also be
pretty cool for your team.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:47.789
So imagine you are a consultant.

00:02:47.789 --> 00:02:49.770
Your partner has a meeting
with a board member

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:50.820
later that afternoon,

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:53.890
and you have the Google alert
activated and get the news.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:56.885
So there's a new article that
was released in the local

00:02:56.885 --> 00:02:59.400
press of where the company is from.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.086
Here it can be a pretty cool
move to be the one who first

00:03:02.086 --> 00:03:05.160
knows about this, shares
the article with the team,

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.193
with the partner,

00:03:07.327 --> 00:03:09.668
and then helping the partner
to have a great meeting

00:03:09.668 --> 00:03:11.302
with the board member,

00:03:11.302 --> 00:03:12.260
because now the partner has an icebreaker

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:14.990
and maybe the article is
even about a difficult topic,

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:17.760
a difficult situation that
the company is facing.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.480
You're for sure it would be important

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:20.680
for your senior leadership,

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:23.360
for your partners to be
aware of what's currently

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:24.750
going on at the client.

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:27.010
And this can be a little
piece of enabling that.

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:30.730
Next tip is to read the
annual report of that company.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:33.320
So if you're not aware an
annual report is a report

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:35.906
that every publicly traded
company needs to release

00:03:35.906 --> 00:03:37.320
once per year.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:40.090
At least in most countries
where they give an overview

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:41.650
about their business activities,

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:44.000
their financials, their strategy.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.607
It's really super insightful

00:03:45.607 --> 00:03:47.730
and a great source of information.

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:50.440
You can usually find annual
reports in the investor

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:53.430
relations section of
the company's website,

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:56.820
or if you just Google annual
report plus the company name,

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:58.200
usually it will directly pop up.

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:00.910
Information that's typically
included in these reports

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:03.400
are information on the
overall company strategy.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:06.070
Some key business results
that were achieved,

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:07.820
future focus initiatives,

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:10.590
what the company wants to
accomplish in the future

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:13.109
and report on industry trends
and business risks that

00:04:13.109 --> 00:04:14.880
the company is facing,

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:16.110
information on personnel

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:18.130
and also remuneration of these people.

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:20.628
And also basic financial, such
as profit and loss statement,

00:04:20.628 --> 00:04:23.570
cashflow statement, balance sheet,

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:26.630
and often also all types
of other pro-forma ratios.

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:29.110
These reports are usually
extremely detailed

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:31.204
and really a great source of
information also with info

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:35.260
on competitors, on
overarching industry trends.

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:38.200
So definitely something that
can inspire many other types of

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:39.470
analysis that you also do.

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:42.490
Next is a tip which is maybe
the most insightful one

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:44.610
and can give you access to information,

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:46.750
which is not that easily
found for instance

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:48.410
when just Googling certain things.

