00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:13.843
But let's continue.

00:06:14.837 --> 00:06:16.860
And as I said, the next tip
I find especially insightful

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:19.695
and this is leveraging
local business registers.

00:06:19.695 --> 00:06:22.810
Because while annual reports are great

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:25.440
they're often only available
really for the largest

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:28.800
publicly traded, publicly
listed companies.

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:30.330
But even for the smaller ones

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:33.290
many of them need to
release business information

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:34.570
on a regular basis.

00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:37.100
And this is exactly what
you can get access on

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:39.100
on these local business registers.

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:41.140
These registers will have different names

00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:43.159
in different countries.

00:06:43.159 --> 00:06:44.720
In Germany for instance
it's the Bundesanzeiger.

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:47.840
But usually if you just
type company register

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:50.070
and then your country into Google,

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:53.080
you will likely find the
name of the company register

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:56.520
of your country and then can
search for it in a similar way.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:58.537
Similar to annual reports
these company registers often

00:06:58.537 --> 00:07:01.282
contain information on financials.

00:07:01.282 --> 00:07:03.810
They often contain the last audit reports.

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:06.200
They might contain information
on the ownership structure

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:08.500
on the management team
and an employee figures.

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:10.560
Often this information
is less detailed than

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:13.200
in the annual reports and
the wealth of information

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:15.818
that needs to be released often
depends on the company size.

00:07:15.818 --> 00:07:19.100
So you often have different
levels of detail available

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:21.598
depending on which type of company

00:07:21.598 --> 00:07:22.639
exactly you're looking at.

00:07:22.639 --> 00:07:24.570
And what makes these registers
even more powerful is that

00:07:24.570 --> 00:07:26.999
nowadays there are all types
of meta registers or types of

00:07:26.999 --> 00:07:31.999
meta search machines that have
connections to have run of

00:07:32.024 --> 00:07:33.460
these local country registers

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:35.550
and then combine all the information.

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:39.500
So for the EU for Europe it's
for instance NorthData.com.

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:41.922
You can just type in the name of a person

00:07:41.922 --> 00:07:44.780
or type in the name of a company,

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:46.900
and you get all types of information

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:48.660
also from different countries here.

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:50.310
So if you're ever interested for instance

00:07:50.310 --> 00:07:53.193
in the business activity of
any of your family members

00:07:53.193 --> 00:07:55.090
or relatives or friends,

00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:58.210
you can just type in the
name of that person into

00:07:58.210 --> 00:07:59.930
for instance NorthData.com

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:02.670
and you see all the companies
they are affiliated to,

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:05.570
wherever they're managing
director on similar positions.

00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:08.030
This is all the information
that you will have.

00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:09.670
So just for demonstration purposes

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:13.300
probably most of you will
know the YouTuber Ali Abdaal.

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:15.334
Ali if you're watching this,

00:08:15.334 --> 00:08:16.610
love your content, great channel.

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:20.380
So if you just try out typing
his name into NorthData,

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:23.340
you see now all the
companies that he has founded

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:24.880
to set up his businesses,

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:27.540
but of course you can also do
this with actual companies.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:29.680
So for instance you could type in Zeeman's

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:32.630
and then really get access
to a plethora of information

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:36.330
that I trust to really help
you to understand what exactly

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:38.350
happened with this
organization in the past,

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:41.610
what was going on and do
some research based on that.

00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:44.270
Last but not least let's
talk about the importance of

00:08:44.270 --> 00:08:45.920
researching industry trends.

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:48.780
So here I trust it's not even
that difficult to do that.

00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:51.300
You can just type the industry of interest

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:53.990
plus industry trends in
the Google search bar,

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:55.550
and then get all types of reports.

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:58.314
As stated earlier you can
also use annual reports

00:08:58.314 --> 00:09:00.040
to really get this information,

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:02.950
read what the company themselves
are writing about this.

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:05.340
So I rather want to talk
about why this is so great

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:06.910
and why this is so important.

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:10.640
And from my experience researching
industry trends are great

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:13.100
icebreakers in conversations with clients.

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:15.220
So for instance in the
construction industry,

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:17.540
which is the industry
that I currently work in,

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:20.870
there's at the moment a
huge shortage of wood.

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:22.820
So let's imagine you're
a consultant or working

00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:24.180
for a construction company.

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:26.040
So in one of the first
meetings with your clients

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:28.800
you could ask them you know
there's this huge shortage

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:32.160
in wood, how is this affecting
your company at the moment?

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:33.900
What does this mean to you?

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:37.320
This can really be a great
icebreaker for your conversation.

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:39.100
And the best thing is
that things like this

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:41.510
also portray you as knowledgeable.

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:43.837
If you openly talk about
industry trends like this,

00:09:43.837 --> 00:09:47.010
surely you know something
about the industry,

00:09:47.010 --> 00:09:49.360
surely you're more than
just the young graduate

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:52.060
fresh out of university who has no clue

00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:53.830
what he or she is doing, right?

00:09:53.830 --> 00:09:56.320
So these are the little
tricks that help you in

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:57.860
conversations with clients.

00:09:57.860 --> 00:10:00.690
Researching the industry,
being able to share little bits

00:10:00.690 --> 00:10:03.030
and pieces like this can
really make the difference

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:04.600
in how you're perceived by your clients

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:06.850
and are able to beat client relationships.

